00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:07.690
things that we're
learning about ourselves,

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:09.670
et cetera, et cetera.

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:12.750
But I thought a good
thing we could start with

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:16.910
s the fact that we recently
went to a concert together

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:17.990
with our wives.

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:19.360
Yeah we did.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:22.920
We went to see Lord Huron.
Lord Huron.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:24.920
In the Hollywood Forever Cemetery.

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:26.640
You can go.
Shout out to Lord Huron.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:27.933
I'm a huge fan.

00:01:29.870 --> 00:01:31.820
And then we saw him in the cemetery

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:36.410
which the vibe kind of fits
a cemetery vibe, it's like.

00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:37.530
The vibe of their music?

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.894
A little bit.

00:01:38.894 --> 00:01:39.727
Yeah I mean I wouldn't say it's creepy

00:01:39.727 --> 00:01:41.550
but there's some haunting,

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:43.950
there's a haunting aspect to it.

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:44.783
For sure.

00:01:44.783 --> 00:01:47.980
Like a Western haunted type thing.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:48.910
Yeah and we are in the West.
That I like.

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:51.700
And that the reverb only
makes it more haunting

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:54.320
but I had never been to the
Hollywood Forever Cemetery.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:55.310
Well I'd seen a movie there

00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:57.610
because they will show
movies there in the same spot

00:01:57.610 --> 00:02:00.180
that they do the concert
which is that big lawn

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:01.110
and there's a giant,

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:03.690
I think it's actually maybe a mausoleum.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.170
Yeah.
That we're.

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:07.090
So they will project a movie.

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:08.690
I call them dead people drawers.

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:10.750
They will project a movie onto the

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.910
dead people drawer building.
Oh.

00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:15.210
But then Lord Huron just
stood right in front of it,

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:16.690
on a stage.

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:18.750
With no, it's the first
time I've been to a concert

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:21.050
where I was that far away
and there was no screen.

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:22.730
It's not, it's just about the sounds man.

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:23.573
And the ambience.
And there's no,

00:02:23.573 --> 00:02:26.770
it's a cemetery that has
not been made into a place

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:27.603
to play music.

00:02:27.603 --> 00:02:31.880
So the only light is
coming from the stage.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:33.124
Did you notice that?

00:02:33.124 --> 00:02:35.130
So walking out of there it was like,

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:36.490
I mean when we were packing up,

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:38.480
you turned on your iPhone light.

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:40.097
That's right, yeah.

00:02:40.097 --> 00:02:40.990
Just to find your stuff.

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:42.940
And there were, we got there kind of late.

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:45.450
We were at the back of the main lawn area

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:47.150
and then there's a walking path

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:49.470
