just lounging on graves.

00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:58.024
Yeah, right.
Checking out the concert.

00:02:58.024 --> 00:02:59.809
I don't know if you're
supposed to do that.

00:02:59.809 --> 00:03:01.700
I mean some people believe
you shouldn't walk.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.100
They're none the wiser.
Walk across a grave.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.210
But I would've thought

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:05.340
that maybe it would've been.
Just lounging.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:06.977
There would've been a sign that says,

00:03:06.977 --> 00:03:09.356
"Don't lounge on the graves."

00:03:09.356 --> 00:03:12.730
But maybe they just thought
that people would know that.

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:14.640
Yeah, it seems like
something you kind of know.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:17.950
But I mean when the place
is full and you're there.

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:19.010
You gotta.
Where else you gonna go?

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:20.500
You gotta prop up somewhere.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:21.923
But when we parked,

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:27.150
I got the special ticket to park inside

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:29.090
which I didn't know that meant just like,

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:33.180
as parking along with the gravestones

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:37.100
as if I was going to a graveside service.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:39.100
They're directing us all the way through.

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:42.610
We got to kind of see
a lot of the graveyard.

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:45.897
There's some famous people buried there.

00:03:45.897 --> 00:03:48.080
The most recent of which that I know of,

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:50.210
Chris Cornell I was just reading about.

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:51.050
I wish we would've found

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:52.340
his gravestone.
Really?

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:55.980
But the thing that is
also significant about it

00:03:55.980 --> 00:04:00.230
that we learned is that the
Hollywood Forever Cemetery

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:04.230
