00:04:47.374 --> 00:04:49.380
Like a photo.
Sometimes more than

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:52.470
an etching.
Photorealistic etching.

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:54.838
Sometimes you're saying a photo.

00:04:54.838 --> 00:04:56.140
Like a printed photo almost.

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:59.160
Of the dead person's face.
Sometimes in color.

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:00.900
Really impressive.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.330
A little creepy.

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:07.122
I mean I kind of thought as I
was walking by some of them,

00:05:07.122 --> 00:05:08.797
you know when you're walking
by a painting it's like,

00:05:08.797 --> 00:05:10.900
"Is she watching me?"

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:13.320
But I think that's just a principle of

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:14.730
if the.
Two dimensions.

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:18.320
If the subject is looking
at the camera lens

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:23.320
or the simulated camera
lens of a artistic painting.

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:26.020
They are technically following you.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:28.520
Yeah, whenever you stand
they're gonna be looking at you

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:29.760
and that doesn't mean they're a ghost.

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:31.250
That just means it's a painting.

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:32.810
It's just how physics works.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:33.750
Or a photo.

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:37.240
But in a normal cemetery,
maybe like you know,

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:41.180
if you're going down Highway
55 on the way to Angier

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:42.797
from Fuquay-Varina.

00:05:42.797 --> 00:05:43.630
Yeah.
I'm just gonna use that

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:44.463
as a normal cemetery.

00:05:44.463 --> 00:05:45.296
Yeah.
There might be

00:05:45.296 --> 00:05:47.924
a couple of people who
have paid a little extry.

00:05:47.924 --> 00:05:49.797
It's like oh he got his face.

00:05:49.797 --> 00:05:50.630
Got his face on there.

00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:52.580
But like you said, almost everyone,

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:55.190
